<title>TURKEY: Turkish central bank reserve fell last week.</title>
<headline>Turkish central bank reserve fell last week.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Thursday its foreign currency reserve fell by $266 million to $16.108 billion in the week ending February 21.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollar</p>
<p>			  February 21   January 14    End-1996</p>
<p> Forex reserve	  16.108	 16.374	16.491</p>
<p> Gold reserve	    1.383	  1.383	 1.383</p>
<p> Total reserve	  17.491	 17.757	17.784</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, fell by $26 million to $26.982 billion in the week ending February 7, the bank said.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
